{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3c5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c40c-7a6a-7610-adaa-109852fda585"},"sequence":61,"recorded_at":1780531400000117,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c40c-b52e-7553-8b1f-5afe694df151"},"task_id":"01a0c40c-b52e-7553-8b1f-5afe694df151","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c40c-b52e-7553-8b1f-5afe694df151","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_reviewer-cr2.md`.\n1|Independently review Change Request revision 2 of TASK-260830-35urbp (implement-private-tmux-server-management), the FIRST of three leaves of STORY-260830-2t4g7i (production-tmux-backend; the chain is 35urbp -> 1c28dz -> g0pcnt). Change Request shape: task_delta on the Story branch (trunk base 799c338; checkpointed predecessors none; tip 799c338e401fca0b24859c0b870cd665927209f2), published by RUN-260921-6e7be5 on muse-spark max, 22 changed paths, patch and validation log attached as TASK-260830-35urbp_change-request_rev2.patch / _rev2-validation.log. Revisions 1..1 are earlier construction attempts of the same producer scope that failed the Change Request validation suite on the pre-PR51 10m race-test timeout under concurrent suites; they carry no review verdict and no prior review findings — review revision 2 on its own merits.. Read the producer brief TASK-260830-35urbp_producer.md, the outcome TASK-260830-35urbp_results.md, TASK-260830-35urbp_conformance-matrix.md, TASK-260830-35urbp_producer-evidence.tar.gz, the CR patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes.\n2|\n3|NORMATIVE AUTHORITY: the pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` **§4.2 tmux backend** (lines 1403-1449), with §4.C (1082), §4.D (1220) and §4.E (1309) as context. The task record's Scope still names v0.5.0 and that is stale — if the candidate cites a v0.5.0 line number or quotes text that is not in the pinned file, that is a finding. Derive every expectation from the spec text, never from a production constant.\n4|\n5|Verify with your own instruments, on isolated immutable copies of the exact candidate tree; never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration.\n6|\n7|(1) **The dedicated-server rule, per vector.** \"AX MUST use its dedicated `-S` server and MUST NOT discover or reuse the operator's default tmux server by ambient socket name\" is not one gate. Drive each vector separately — an environment variable naming a socket, an inherited socket, a default path, a conventional name — and for each, assert the refusal at the production entry the matrix names. A candidate that closes one vector and reports the class is the single most likely shape here; census the call sites and plant a fresh spelling that walks through.\n8|\n9|(2) **The background-caller rules, which are the hard part.** A Background caller MUST NOT create a credential-dependent tmux server. A background CLI, SSH RPC process, daemon or restore worker MAY contact an already-running authenticated broker and its attested server, and if neither exists it MUST return `capability_unavailable` with typed realm/readiness details and MUST NOT fall back to direct server creation. Plant a direct-creation call on the background path and require a committed test to redden; a fall-back prohibition implemented as a comment, a doc line or an unreachable branch is a P1. Assert the LITERAL token `capability_unavailable` and the typed realm/readiness detail, not `== pkg.SomeConst` — swap the constant to another registered value with the same exit and see whether the suite notices.\n10|\n11|(3) **`launchctl managername` is a diagnostic hint only, and a cached sentinel or prior observation MUST NOT authorize.** This is exactly the shape that has been faked on this epic before with a reflection census of field names. Drive a cached/stale observation into the production entry and assert it authorizes nothing; a name census is not an effect census.\n12|\n13|(4) **Owner-only runtime directories.** Mode, ownership and containment are three gates. Check specifically that path logic delegates to the landed `internal/secprim` openat-relative walk rather than re-implementing containment: lexical containment plus `O_NOFOLLOW` is not containment, a symlinked intermediate escapes it, and a check after `open()` never runs on a FIFO. Plant a symlinked intermediate component and a FIFO.\n14|\n15|(5) **The determinism constraint, verified not read.** The brief required every rule to be driven to its effect by a committed test that passes with NO tmux process anywhere, with any real-tmux test separately gated and never the only witness for an acceptance row. Verify it by running the suite in an environment where tmux cannot be reached (make the binary unresolvable in your isolated copy) and reporting exactly which tests fail or skip. A row whose only witness skips in that run is an unmeasured row, however green the producer's log looks. Also check the converse: a rule degraded into a mock-only shape so it could be tested is a finding, not a solution — the production entry must still be the thing under test.\n16|\n17|(6) **No forked owners.** `internal/terminalbackend`, `internal/axpane`, `internal/terminstance`, `internal/termbind`, `internal/secprim`, `internal/environ`, `internal/canonicaljson`, `internal/scalar` are landed. Grep for a second model of anything they already own (string bounds in characters not bytes, uint53 and the AX number model, digests, sorted-unique arrays, closed-shape decoding, argv and path safety). The results must name which existing type or gate was extended; verify that claim rather than accepting it — \"composes X\" and \"nothing re-implemented\" are censusable claims.\n18|\n19|(7) **Traceability boundary.** This leaf must NOT touch `internal/traceability` (registry, digest pin, README measured-coverage subsection) — that belongs to the final leaf g0pcnt. Any edit there is a finding. Package-local TRACEABILITY.md and the conformance matrix are the right places.\n20|\n21|(8) **Mutation and hygiene.** Rerun the shipped harness in an isolated copy, rerun each KILLED twice, and plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on gates the producer did not mutate, plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control. Per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators; NOT_APPLIED is not a pass. `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; zero `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in the CR tree or your copies. gofmt/vet clean. The candidate must be byte-identical to trunk everywhere outside this leaf's scope — check every path in `git diff --name-only <the CR base> <current origin/main>` that also appears in the candidate, because a refresh carries stale pre-refresh copies that read as reverts. Crash and idempotency evidence is required for every durable write (a runtime directory and a server socket are durable writes) or an explicit purity bound. The full configured suite must be green on the exact tree; read the command count from the candidate config rather than assuming a number.\n22|\n23|Report the coverage ratio YOU measured against the acceptance table's real row count, not the producer's restated one. Attach TASK-260830-35urbp_review-verdict-rev2.md and TASK-260830-35urbp_review-evidence-rev2.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), complete the live merged checklist, then `accept_cr(TASK-260830-35urbp, revision=2, evidence=TASK-260830-35urbp_review-verdict-rev2.md)` or hand off changes requested with P1/P2/P3 classes named and a short \"Rework scope (for the producer)\" section at the end. Model: claude-opus-5 max. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.","final_result":true}}}
