| `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...` exit 0 on the candidate copy; `runtime_test.go` carries `//go:build !windows`; `ownership_windows.go` stub compiles the shared files |\n47|| P1-B forked attestation gate | **yes** | `LiveAttestation`/`CachedObservation`/`ManagerNameHint`/`BrokerStatus`/`Request.Hint`/`Cached`/`NeedsCredentials` have zero occurrences in the package or README. `RealmAdmission` = `terminalbackend.Admitted` + `RawGeneration`; `CheckServerAttested` = `Admitted.Has(\"credential_capable_execution_realm\") && RawGeneration == Generation`, the same two arms `axpane.checkRealm` (decide.go:913-928) applies; the host-binding/provider-build cross-bind is stated as B13. The three rev1 holes now refuse through `Acquire`: wrong-generation foreground attach (`TestAcquireForegroundRefusesWrongGenerationAdmission`), wrong-generation broker (`.../stale_server_admission`), and the replayed-cached shape is no longer expressible — a stale admission refuses on the generation arm. Broker principal is typed (`UID` + `Generation`), both arms pinned (N-broker-uid, N-broker-generation, my R06 at the entry wiring) |\n48|| P2-A nine surviving narrowings | **yes** | Each has a committed killer and a shipped row; all KILLED in both of my harness passes: N-acquire-commit-refusal, N-containment-symlink-verify, N-override-tmpdir, N-collision-{inherited,tmuxenv,tmpdir,conventional}, N-argv-tmuxenv, N-fchmod-umask. The unreachable `ObserveAmbient` vocabulary arm is deleted (`secprim` import gone from socket.go) |\n49|| P2-B Windows arm | **yes** | `lexicalRuntimePath` refuses `PlatformWindows` on every host (`TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesWindowsOnUnixHost`, `TestAcquireRefusesWindowsPlatform`, N-platform-windows); Windows commit/verify arms are refusal stubs; tripwire and `_ = filepath.Clean` gone |\n50|| P2-C adapter bound | **yes** | B9 stated; the \"Production wires live tmux and broker probes\" sentence is gone (acquire.go:57-64 now says no production probe/spawner exists) |\n51|| P2-D dead inputs / Verify contradiction | **yes** | dead members deleted; foreground `checkCreationAllowed` call deleted; background calls `VerifyRuntimeDir` (`TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` asserts no directory and no probe; my R25 re-plants Ensure on that path → KILLED; my R07 reorders probe-before-verify → KILLED) |\n52|| P3-A suite key | **yes** | results read the right key; all 30 reported as run firsthand, consistent with the attached logs |\n53|| P3-B umask bound | **yes** | B10; my probe P19 confirms a stranded 0600 leaf refuses `runtime mode` on every retry |\n54|| P3-C symlinked root intermediate | **yes** | B11; my probe P07 confirms the intermediate is followed and the leaf lands under the target |\n55|| P3-D CheckArgv arm | **yes** | `TestBuildArgvRefusesInvalidArgvShape` + B12 + N-argv-shape |\n56|\n57|## P2 — must fix or state as a bound\n58|\n59|### P2-A. The verify-side \"non-directory leaf\" refusal is unpinned: the background production path admits a regular file as the runtime directory and hangs on a FIFO under a one-flag narrowing\n60|\n61|Row 5 (\"Non-directory leaf refuses\") names `EnsureRuntimeDir` only. The verify side implements\n62|the same refusal through the `O_DIRECTORY` flag on `verifyRuntimeDir`'s `Openat`\n63|(runtime_unix.go:105-106), and that side is what `Acquire` uses on the background path\n64|(acquire.go:168). No committed test stages a non-directory leaf against `VerifyRuntimeDir` or\n65|the background `Acquire`, and no harness row narrows that flag. Reviewer plant\n66|`R01-verify-odirectory` (drop `O_DIRECTORY` from the verify `Openat`, keep `O_NOFOLLOW`):\n67|\n68|- against the committed suite as shipped (full package, no `-run` mask): **SURVIVED** in both\n69|  passes (`reviewer-battery-pass{1,2}/R01-verify-odirectory.committed.log`, exit 0);\n70|- with my probes present: **KILLED** — `TestReviewProbeVerifyRegularFileLeafRefuses` (a\n71|  regular 0700 file at `root/ax-tmux` → `VerifyRuntimeDir` returns nil) and\n72|  `TestReviewProbeFIFOLeafVerifyRefusesWithoutBlocking` (a FIFO at the leaf → `VerifyRuntimeDir`\n73|  **blocks for the full 5s deadline**, because the verify `Openat` carries no `O_NONBLOCK`; the\n74|  landed `secprim.openNoFollow` comment documents exactly this hang class)\n75|  (`R01-verify-odirectory.with-probe.log`).\n76|\n77|The commit side is pinned by reroute (`TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` asserts the\n78|`runtime containment` detail; dropping `O_DIRECTORY` there reroutes to `runtime mode`). This is\n79|the rev1 P2-A shape \"the verify side follows a symlink leaf\" recurring one member over: the\n80|symlink member got its verify-side test and row (`TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkLeaf`,\n81|N-containment-symlink-verify), the non-directory member did not. Production is correct today\n82|(my probes P04-P06 show FIFO leaf/root refuse on both entries without blocking), but the DoD\n83|line \"refusing behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must\n84|reject\" is not met on the entry the background path uses.\n85|\n86|Fix: a committed `TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` (regular file, and a FIFO under\n87|a deadline so the no-hang property is pinned too), the same shape driven through the background\n88|`Acquire` (my `TestReviewProbeBackgroundRegularFileLeafRefusesThroughAcquire` is the template),\n89|and a harness row `N-containment-odirectory-verify` that drops the flag on the verify `Openat`\n90|only. Update row 5 to name both entries.\n91|\n92|## P3 — fix in the same rework\n93|\n94|- **P3-A. Both-empty generation arms are unmeasured on two exported entries.**\n95|  `CheckServerAttested`'s `wantGeneration == \"\"` disjunct (readiness.go:43) and\n96|  `CheckBrokerContact`'s `report.Principal.Generation == \"\"` disjunct (readiness.go:83) survive\n97|  deletion against the committed suite (`R02-attested-empty-generation`,\n98|  `R03-broker-empty-generation`: SURVIVED ×2, exit 0). Every committed row keeps one side\n99|  non-empty, so `\"\" != \"generation-7\"` refuses with or without the arm; the arm is load-bearing\n100|  only for the both-empty pair, which my probes P10/P11 drive (`RealmAdmission{Admitted:\n101|  realm}` with want `\"\"` → admitted under the mutant). Through `Acquire` the pair is unreachable\n102|  (the typed-details check refuses an empty `Generation` first, pinned by R20a), so this is\n103|  confined to direct callers of the exported helpers. One both-empty row in each table closes\n104|  it, or state the arm as entry-unreachable.\n105|- **P3-B. \"Exactly 0700\" is pinned on the widened side only.** `R11a-mode-narrower-create` and\n106|  `R11b-mode-narrower-verify` (`Perm() != 0o700` → `Perm()&0o077 != 0`, admitting owner-narrower\n107|  modes such as 0600/0500) SURVIVED ×2 against the committed suite and are KILLED by my probes\n108|  P19/P24 (a pre-existing 0600 leaf → both entries return nil under the mutant). Not a\n109|  confidentiality exposure — a narrower mode exposes nothing — but doc.go, README, TRACEABILITY\n110|  rows 1/4 and the runtime.go comment say \"exact\"/\"exactly 0700\". Either pin the narrower side\n111|  (a pre-existing 0600 leaf refuses `runtime mode` on Ensure and Verify) or restate the claim as\n112|  \"no group/world bits\" (mode ⊆ 0700) so prose and tests agree.\n113|- **P3-C. The collision gate is byte equality, not path equality.** `checkAmbientDisjoint`\n114|  (socket.go:103) compares strings. An ambient value naming the derived socket through an\n115|  unclean spelling (`dir/./ax-tmux.sock`, `dir//ax-tmux.sock`) or through a symlinked alias of\n116|  the root walks past every member (probes P01-P03: `Acquire` spawns). Row 23's \"colliding with\n117|  the derived socket refuses on every member\" holds for byte-identical values only. The spec\n118|  rule is unaffected — the socket is derived, never selected from an ambient value — so this\n119|  is a package-local defense-in-depth claim that outruns its tests: either `filepath.Clean`\n120|  both sides (symlink aliases remain a bound) or state the byte-equality bound in TRACEABILITY.\n121|- **P3-D. LOGBOOK carries a rev1 entry describing code that never reached trunk.** LOGBOOK.md\n122|  lines 14-22 (the \"TASK-260830-35urbp — Private tmux server management\" block under the rev2\n123|  block) still say `CheckLiveAttestation` \"admits only complete live sentinel+smoke\", \"all four\n124|  ambient vectors\", \"Windows ownership is the creating-user ACL (tripwire-pinned)\", \"29\n125|  narrowing mutants\", \"54 of 54 rows\", \"87.5% statement coverage\" — every one of these\n126|  describes the rejected rev1 tree. Neither entry has landed; landing both records a design\n127|  that was deleted before it existed on trunk. Fold the rev1 block into the rev2 block (keep\n128|  F1-F3 as the findings they are) or mark it superseded in place.\n129|- **P3-E. Fail-closed error arms that are prose only.** `handleBoundToPath`'s two stat-failure\n130|  arms (\"an unreadable root fails closed into the mismatch refusal\", runtime.go:127-139) flip\n131|  to fail-open under `R10-handle-stat-fail-open` and SURVIVE — no test can stage a `Stat`\n132|  failure on an open directory handle without a seam, so the sentence is unmeasured (rejection\n133|  pattern f). Same class: `verifyOwnership`'s `!ok` arm (\"a stat without ownership metadata\n134|  fails closed\", ownership_unix.go:29-34), unstageable on unix. State both as bounds\n135|  (unmeasured error arms, no seam) or add the seam. Reported honestly as an error-arm row, not\n136|  counted as a narrowing survivor.\n137|\n138|## Observations (not findings; worth a sentence in TRACEABILITY if the producer agrees)\n139|\n140|- The no-fallback proof covers spawns routed through `Dependencies.Spawn` (D-background-fallback\n141|  and my R14 both KILLED by the zero-call spies). A fallback through a direct `os/exec` call is\n142|  outside the injected model and is excluded today only by the import census (no `os/exec`\n143|  import in the package) — a fact worth stating under B9.\n144|- The mode gate reads permission bits only: setgid/sticky bits on a 0700 leaf are admitted\n145|  (probe P08) and macOS ACLs are not inspected. This matches the landed `hosttrust` custody\n146|  precedent (`custody_unix.go:15`, `Perm() == mode`), so it is the same bound, not a fork.\n147|- The derived socket path is not checked against the platform `sun_path` limit (104 bytes on\n148|  macOS); a deep state root will surface as a spawn failure in the lifecycle leaf's adapter.\n149|\n150|## §M — reviewer battery (16 rows, two passes, `reviewer_battery.py` in the evidence archive)\n151|\n152|Every row: anchor count verified (all 16 applied, none NOT_APPLIED), plant applied to the\n153|mutant copy, the committed suite run as shipped (full package, no `-run` mask), exit + raw\n154|output logged, file restored, tree re-hashed to `19820613` after each pass. Rows predicted\n155|SURVIVED were additionally run with my probe file present and the named killer selected.\n156|\n157|| Row | Kind | Gate (site) | Committed suite | With probe | Killer |\n158|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n159|| R01-verify-odirectory | narrowing | verify Openat drops `O_DIRECTORY` (runtime_unix.go:106) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | P09 regular file admitted; P05 FIFO **blocks 5s** |\n160|| R02-attested-empty-generation | narrowing | `wantGeneration == \"\"` arm (readiness.go:43) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | P10 |\n161|| R03-broker-empty-generation | narrowing | `Principal.Generation == \"\"` arm (readiness.go:83) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | P11 |\n162|| R05-unattested-as-absent | narrowing | `if report.Running` gains `&& Has(realm)` (acquire.go:210) | KILLED | — | TestAcquireForegroundRefusesRunningUnattested |\n163|| R06-broker-uid-self | narrowing | entry passes `status.Principal.UID` as the current UID (acquire.go:175) | KILLED | — | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/foreign-user_broker |\n164|| R07-probe-before-verify | additive | broker probed before custody verify (acquire.go:168) | KILLED | — | TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating, TestAcquireBackgroundStagesVerifyCustodyRefusal |\n165|| R08-silent-repair | narrowing | `if created` → always chmod (runtime_unix.go:54) | KILLED | — | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesWidenedMode, TestAcquireForegroundStagesCommitPhaseCustodyRefusal |\n166|| R09-ensure-before-override | additive | foreground Ensure before the override refusal (acquire.go:147) | KILLED | — | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector (all 5 subtests) |\n167|| R10-handle-stat-fail-open | error-arm | stat-failure arms return true (runtime.go:133,138) | **SURVIVED** | (no killer possible without a seam) | — |\n168|| R11a-mode-narrower-create | narrowing | create-side `Perm()&0o077 != 0` (runtime_unix.go:73) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | P19 |\n169|| R11b-mode-narrower-verify | narrowing | verify-side `Perm()&0o077 != 0` (runtime_unix.go:116) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | P24 |\n170|| R14-linux-miss-fallback | additive | non-macOS background miss spawns directly (acquire.go:185) | KILLED | — | TestAcquireBackgroundMissOnLinuxAlsoRefusesWithoutFallback |\n171|| R20a-details-generation | narrowing | typed-details arm drops `Generation == \"\"` (acquire.go:140) | KILLED | — | TestAcquireRefusesMissingRealmDetails/generation |\n172|| R20b-details-broker | narrowing | typed-details arm drops `BrokerState == \"\"` | KILLED | — | TestAcquireRefusesMissingRealmDetails/broker_state |\n173|| R25-background-ensures | narrowing | background calls Ensure instead of Verify (acquire.go:168) | KILLED | — | TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating |\n174|| C-reviewer-control | control | comment-only edit in socket.go | SURVIVED | — | (must survive; proves the battery observes outcomes) |\n175|\n176|Denominator: 16 applied rows (12 narrowing, 3 additive, 1 error-arm) + 1 control. Of the 12\n177|narrowings, 7 KILLED by the committed suite, 5 SURVIVED and are each proven real by a probe\n178|kill. Every KILLED row was killed by exactly the test named above (kill lines in the raw logs).\n179|\n180|## §P — reviewer probes (27, `probes-rev2.log`)\n181|\n182|P01-P03 collision unclean/doubled/symlink spellings admitted (P3-C); P04-P06 FIFO leaf (Ensure,\n183|Verify) and FIFO root refuse `runtime containment` within the deadline — no hang; P07 B11\n184|confirmed; P08 setgid/sticky admitted; P09/P09b regular-file leaf refuses on Verify and on the\n185|background `Acquire` (baselines for R01); P10/P11 both-empty generation pairs refuse (baselines\n186|for R02/R03); P12 a request generation newer than the live broker's refuses\n187|`capability_unavailable` carrying the request's generation; P13 foreground never probes the\n188|broker; P14 backslash name refuses; P15 trailing-slash root refuses `runtime root`; P16\n189|whitespace override refuses; P17 background foreign-ownership refuses through `Acquire` before\n190|the broker is probed; P18 5000/100000-char remediation still renders the typed unavailable\n191|(axerror admits them), invalid UTF-8 and NUL reach the constructor-failure arm and refuse\n192|`tmux_invalid_arguments realm details` (fail-closed, never nil); P19 stranded 0600 leaf never\n193|converges (B10); P20 read-only root refuses `runtime commit` (uncovered Mkdirat arm is\n194|fail-closed); P21 broker hit carries the derived socket and no argv; P22 a superset Admitted\n195|admits (Has semantics); P23 umask 0077 converges; P24 narrower leaf refuses on Verify; P25\n196|uppercase UUID refused by the landed grammar (no canonicalization gap); P26 the SIGKILL child\n197|leaves the mkdirat-committed leaf and the retry verifies it (crash test shape genuine).\n198|\n199|## What held under attack (keep)\n200|\n201|- Dedicated-server rule per vector: override refused on all five members through `Acquire`\n202|  with no spawn and no directory; collision refused on all five (byte-identical); argv gate\n203|  refuses all five; `Acquire` never reads the environment (no `Getenv`/`Environ`/`exec` in any\n204|  production file; socket.go imports `path/filepath` only).\n205|- Background rules: broker-or-refuse with the literal `capability_unavailable`, exit 6, and the\n206|  five typed details asserted as literals; no fallback along the caller (N-creation-literal),\n207|  platform (R14, my plant) and spawner (D-background-fallback) axes; verify-never-create on the\n208|  authorizing path (R25, R07); same-user and generation-bound broker principal at the entry\n209|  (R06).\n210|- Attestation: landed `terminalbackend.Admitted` consumed through `Has`, composed with the\n211|  generation equality axpane enforces; stale admissions refuse on both paths; decoy capability\n212|  refuses; Windows refuses on every host.\n213|- Custody: FIFO leaf/root and symlink leaf/root refuse on both entries without blocking; widened\n214|  mode, foreign UID and handle mismatch refuse on both entries; the explicit `Fchmod` is\n215|  load-bearing under umask 0177; the real-SIGKILL crash test is genuine (P26).\n216|- No forks: `axpane` caller vocabulary, `axerror` typed refusal, `scalar` grammars, `secprim`\n217|  Guard/OpenNoFollowDir/CheckArgv, `terminalbackend.Admitted` — all consumed; `handleBoundToPath`\n218|  mirrors the private `secprim.guardRootMatches` and says so.\n219|- Determinism: 0 SKIP with tmux unresolvable; no real-tmux witness (B1, honest).\n220|- Boundary: `internal/traceability` untouched; README section carries no CLI/capability claim;\n221|  no trunk drift.\n222|\n223|## Coverage ratio measured against the 55-row table\n224|\n225|**55 of 55 rows are driven as stated** — the ratio is honest, not inflated. The gaps above sit\n226|outside the row statements: row 5 names Ensure only (P2-A), rows 36/38 keep one side non-empty\n227|(P3-A), rows 1/4 claim \"exact\" while pinning widening only (P3-B), row 23 holds for byte-equal\n228|values only (P3-C).\n229|\n230|## Rework scope (for the producer)\n231|\n232|1. **P2-A**: add `TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` (regular 0700 file; plus a FIFO\n233|   leaf under a deadline so the no-hang property is pinned), drive the regular-file shape through\n234|   the background `Acquire`, ship harness row `N-containment-odirectory-verify` (drop\n235|   `O_DIRECTORY` on the verify `Openat` only, expect KILLED), and name both entries in row 5.\n236|2. **P3-A**: one both-empty-generation row in `TestCheckServerAttestedRefusesEachMissingConjunct`\n237|   and one in `TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact`, or state the arms as\n238|   entry-unreachable bounds.\n239|3. **P3-B**: pin a pre-existing 0600 leaf as `runtime mode` on both entries, or restate the mode\n240|   claim as \"no group/world bits\" in doc.go/README/TRACEABILITY/runtime.go.\n241|4. **P3-C**: `filepath.Clean` both sides of `checkAmbientDisjoint` (with a test for `/./` and\n242|   `//` spellings) or state the byte-equality bound; symlink aliases stay a bound either way.\n243|5. **P3-D**: fold or supersede the rev1 LOGBOOK block so no landed entry describes\n244|   `CheckLiveAttestation`, four vectors, the tripwire, 54/54, or 29 mutants.\n245|6. **P3-E**: state the unmeasured stat-failure arms of `handleBoundToPath` and `verifyOwnership`\n246|   as bounds (or add a seam and a row).\n247|7. Rerun the package suite, `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...`, the harness twice, and the\n248|   30-command suite; refresh results/matrix/archive; hand off as revision 3. Everything in \"What\n249|   held under attack\" needs no change — do not re-litigate it.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
