`//go:build !windows` (it reassigns the unix-only `effectiveUID` seam and uses `syscall.Umask`); new `ownership_windows.go` stub keeps shared files compiling | `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...` exit 0 (the gate itself; was failing on rev1) | `logs/windows-vet.log` |\n24|| P1-B forked attestation gate (3 holes) | Deleted `LiveAttestation`/`CachedObservation`/`ManagerNameHint`/`BrokerStatus.Attested` and `Request.Hint`/`Cached`/`NeedsCredentials` with no replacement fields. `RealmAdmission` consumes the landed `terminalbackend.Admitted` verdict composed only with `RawGeneration == Generation`; broker principal is a typed same-user UID plus generation-bound generation | `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesWrongGenerationAdmission`, `TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/stale_server_admission` (foreground + broker wrong-generation holes), `.../foreign-user_broker` (untyped broker hole); each fails if the arm is weakened (see N-rows) | `pkg-tests-v.log`, `harness-pass1/N-realm-*.log`, `harness-pass1/N-broker-*.log` |\n25|| P2-A Acquire swallows commit refusal | Added foreground `Acquire` test staging a widened mode; `Ensure` documents its \"\"-vs-joined failure contract | `TestAcquireForegroundStagesCommitPhaseCustodyRefusal` (mutant probes and spawns past the widened mode) | `harness-pass1/N-acquire-commit-refusal.log` |\n26|| P2-A verify-side symlink fallback | Added verify-side symlink test + shipped row | `TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkLeaf` | `harness-pass1/N-containment-symlink-verify.log` |\n27|| P2-A override admits TMUX_TMPDIR | Fifth override vector (row 55) through `Acquire` and `ResolveSocket` | `TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/tmux_tmpdir` | `harness-pass1/N-override-tmpdir.log` |\n28|| P2-A collision admits one member ×4 | Per-member collision tables through `Acquire` (and direct) | `TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollision` (5 subtests) | `harness-pass1/N-collision-*.log` |\n29|| P2-A argv admits TMUX env value | Fifth argv member | `TestBuildArgvRefusesAmbientSocket/tmux_env_value` | `harness-pass1/N-argv-tmuxenv.log` |\n30|| P2-A Fchmod arm unobserved | umask-0177 create test proving the explicit chmod | `TestEnsureRuntimeDirEnforcesModeUnderRestrictiveUmask` | `harness-pass1/N-fchmod-umask.log` |\n31|| P2-A dead ambient-vocabulary arm | Deleted `ObserveAmbient`'s unreachable `IsEnvName` refusal and its row-18 sentence; `secprim` import removed | — (deletion; row 18 now pins record-without-use only) | `pkg-tests-v.log` (ObserveAmbient tests) |\n32|| P2-B Windows arm claims tmux | `PlatformWindows` refuses at the lexical gate on every host; Windows commit/verify arms are refusal stubs; tripwire and `WindowsBound` deleted; unix host arms deleted (lexical is the single gate) | `TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesWindowsOnUnixHost`, `TestAcquireRefusesWindowsPlatform` | `harness-pass1/N-platform-windows.log`, `logs/windows-vet.log` |\n33|| P2-C missing adapter bound | Stated bound B9; deleted the \"Production wires live tmux and broker probes\" sentence | — (bound, no code to kill) | `TRACEABILITY.md` B9 |\n34|| P2-D dead inputs/arms, Verify contradiction | Deleted `Request.NeedsCredentials`/`Hint`/`Cached`; deleted the dead foreground `checkCreationAllowed` call; background acquisition now calls `VerifyRuntimeDir` (no durable write on the authorizing path) | `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating`, `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesVerifyCustodyRefusal` | `harness-pass1/N-acquire-verify-refusal.log` |\n35|| P3-A suite miscount | Commands read from `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` (30); all 30 run firsthand below | — (reporting fix) | `logs/cmd*.log` |\n36|| P3-B umask-conditional convergence | Stated bound B10 (umask & 0700 == 0) | — (bound) | `TRACEABILITY.md` B10 |\n37|| P3-C symlinked root intermediate | Stated bound B11 (matches secprim's own root open) | — (bound) | `TRACEABILITY.md` B11 |\n38|| P3-D CheckArgv arm uncovered | Covered by direct `BuildArgv` call with its Acquire-unreachability bound B12 | `TestBuildArgvRefusesInvalidArgvShape` | `harness-pass1/N-argv-shape.log` |\n39|\n40|Kept untouched per the verdict: the genuinely pinned no-fallback rule\n41|(caller, credential, platform axes), the custody gates that held under\n42|attack, the FIFO/symlink/mode/UID/handle-mismatch refusals, the\n43|real-SIGKILL crash test, and the `internal/traceability` boundary.\n44|\n45|## Deliverable (rev2 shape)\n46|\n47|`internal/tmuxserver`, composing the landed owners (never forked):\n48|\n49|- (1) Runtime custody: `EnsureRuntimeDir` / `VerifyRuntimeDir` with\n50|  three independent gates (containment, exact `0700`, eUID ownership).\n51|  Foreground acquisition ensures idempotently; background acquisition\n52|  verifies the existing directory and never creates it.\n53|- (2) Dedicated socket: `SocketPath` / `ResolveSocket` derive the one\n54|  `-S` socket and refuse overrides and ambient collisions on all five\n55|  members (TMUX env, TMUX_TMPDIR, inherited socket, default path,\n56|  conventional name).\n57|- (3) Acquisition: `Acquire` refuses malformed input, ambient reuse,\n58|  and missing dependencies before any side effect. Foreground attaches\n59|  or spawns; background brokers-or-refuses with the typed\n60|  `capability_unavailable` and no fallback (the miss path consults the\n61|  creation gate by call; every background test arms a zero-call spy).\n62|- (4) Readiness: `CheckServerAttested` / `CheckBrokerContact` decide\n63|  the landed admission (`Admitted.Has(realm)` + generation equality)\n64|  over a typed same-user generation-bound broker principal. A stale\n65|  admission — the replayed-cached shape — refuses on both paths.\n66|- (5) Spawn argv: `BuildArgv` emits exactly\n67|  `tmux -S socket new-session -d -s session ax pane session`\n68|  through the landed argv gate. Native Windows refuses every request.\n69|\n70|Extended vs deliberately not extended:\n71|\n72|- Extended (composed): `terminalbackend.Admitted` (attestation\n73|  verdict), `axpane` caller vocabulary, `axerror` typed refusal,\n74|  `scalar` platform/path/UUIDv7 grammars, `secprim` Guard /\n75|  `OpenNoFollowDir` / `CheckArgv`, the `hosttrust` verify-never-repair\n76|  precedent, the `termbind` crash-hook pattern.\n77|- Deliberately not extended: `hosttrust` custody itself (Host Channel\n78|  authority — a tmux runtime dir is not a trust store);\n79|  `terminalbackend` Reconcile evidence admission (consumed, not\n80|  re-owned); `axpane` checkRealm (unexported; this leaf composes the\n81|  same Has-plus-generation-equality over the probe-reported verdict);\n82|  the host-binding/provider-build cross-bind (stays with the lifecycle\n83|  owner, bound B13); `terminstance` lifecycle execution (sibling leaf);\n84|  `secprim`'s private `guardRootMatches` (mirrored as\n85|  `handleBoundToPath` with a seam because the original is unexported);\n86|  `internal/traceability` (untouched — bindings and the re-pin belong\n87|  to the final leaf).\n88|\n89|Determinism: every broker, server, and spawner interaction runs\n90|through injected dependencies. No test starts a tmux process; the\n91|suite passes with the tmux binary unresolvable and no tmux process on\n92|the host. No AC row has a real-tmux witness — that is the design, not\n93|a gap (bound B1).\n94|\n95|## Coverage ratio (measured, not planned)\n96|\n97|**55 of 55 AC rows driven** through production entries by named\n98|committed tests — matrix in `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`,\n99|reproduced with spec-clause mapping in\n100|`TASK-260830-35urbp_conformance-matrix.md` (rev2). Row 55 is new: the\n101|fifth override vector the reviewer found unpinned. Rows 24-39 are\n102|re-derived from the composed landed-admission gate; rows 15, 18, 47,\n103|52 are re-derived as the table above describes.\n104|\n105|## Mutants (shipped harness, per-plant raw logs)\n106|\n107|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py` —\n108|40 narrowing + 1 supplementary additive (D-background-fallback,\n109|labeled) + 1 harmless SURVIVED control. Pass 1 and pass 2: **42/42\n110|each, verdict lists identical**, exit 0. Per-row raw logs (go output +\n111|subprocess exit) for both passes are in the evidence tarball;\n112|production blobs byte-identical before/after every run\n113|(`git status` shows only candidate paths). No token-preserving\n114|source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text (stated\n115|bound B4, harness executes the behavioral suite). The one\n116|nil-dependency narrowing that kills by panic (N-deps-foreground) is\n117|disclosed in the harness and the matrix; N-deps-background kills by a\n118|custody-code mismatch since the admitted request reaches Verify.\n119|N-fchmod-umask assumes a non-root test user (bound B14), the same\n120|shape as the reviewer's plant.\n121|\n122|## Crash / idempotency\n123|\n124|Real SIGKILL seam (unix): `TestEnsureCrashChildSelfTerminates`\n125|(child runs the genuine `EnsureRuntimeDir` entry and kills itself in\n126|`AfterMkdir`, after mkdirat and before verification plus parent\n127|fsync; parent proves the retry converges to the one verified\n128|directory). Idempotent replay: `TestEnsureRuntimeDirIsIdempotent`,\n129|`TestAcquireCreatesRuntimeDirIdempotently`,\n130|`TestAcquireForegroundSpawnIsIdempotentAcrossRetry` (spawn-then-retry\n131|attaches with exactly one spawn). Crash convergence states the umask\n132|bound B10; the server socket's crash evidence is owned by the\n133|lifecycle leaf (bound B9).\n134|\n135|## Validation (all run firsthand in this session)\n136|\n137|Configured suite read from `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands`\n138|(count 30, verified by read). All 30 green, run by this run (nothing\n139|accepted from rev1 or from construction):\n140|\n141|- 1 gofmt clean; 2 `go build ./...` exit 0; 3 `go vet ./...` exit 0.\n142|- 4 `go test ./... -count=1 -v` exit 0: 45/45 packages ok, 0 package\n143|  FAIL, 0 unindented test FAIL (the 21 indented `--- FAIL` lines are