{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c697","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c40c-7a6a-7610-adaa-109852fda585"},"sequence":422,"recorded_at":1780531400000839,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c40d-82fd-79e3-abbd-0101bfe2298e"},"task_id":"01a0c40d-82fd-79e3-abbd-0101bfe2298e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c40d-82fd-79e3-abbd-0101bfe2298e","chunk":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/doc.go`.\n1|// Package tmuxserver owns AX private tmux server management: owner-only\n2|// runtime directories and dedicated tmux -S servers with no ambient or\n3|// default-server discovery or reuse. It is the first leaf of the\n4|// production-tmux-backend story.\n5|//\n6|// Normative scope: AX v0.7.0 Section 4.2 (tmux backend, dedicated -S\n7|// server, credential-sensitive creation, background broker-or-refuse,\n8|// launchctl managername as diagnostic hint only, cached observations\n9|// never authorize resume), Section 4.C (operation vocabulary cited for\n10|// the wrapper entrypoint shape only), Section 4.D (capability evidence\n11|// cited landed), and Section 4.E (sensitive runtime state is owner-only\n12|// and non-replicable).\n13|//\n14|// Division of authority (composed, never forked): the caller vocabulary\n15|// (foreground/background) comes from internal/axpane, which already\n16|// gates the wrapper decision over it; the capability_unavailable typed\n17|// refusal comes from internal/axerror.NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable, which\n18|// enforces the exact Section 15.3 detail set; the attestation verdict\n19|// comes from the landed internal/terminalbackend admission\n20|// (Reconcile/ResolveEvidence), consumed here as an Admitted set\n21|// composed only with the generation equality the wrapper owner\n22|// already enforces — sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature\n23|// verification, liveness, and expiry are the admission's verdict, not\n24|// this leaf's; path grammars come from internal/scalar (absolute root,\n25|// relative member, UUIDv7 session); lexical containment comes from\n26|// internal/secprim.Guard; argv shape validation comes from\n27|// internal/secprim.CheckArgv. What this package owns is the composition\n28|// no landed package provides: the descriptor-relative runtime-directory\n29|// commit (mkdirat from a pinned root handle, not a path-string\n30|// MkdirAll), the three independent custody gates (mode, ownership,\n31|// containment), the five-member ambient non-use proof (TMUX and\n32|// TMUX_TMPDIR environment values, inherited socket, default path,\n33|// conventional name), the background broker-or-refuse acquisition path\n34|// with its no-fallback gate over a typed same-user generation-bound\n35|// broker principal, the foreground ensure-then-attach-or-spawn path,\n36|// and the dedicated -S argv builder.\n37|//\n38|// Bounds: no ax CLI surface, no lifecycle operations (create, attach,\n39|// status, quiesce, stop, terminate, restore belong to the sibling\n40|// leaves), no ConPTY process control, no provider process, no mesh\n41|// transport, and no production probe or spawner implementation —\n42|// caller-supplied probes report the landed admission verdicts, and the\n43|// exec/probe adapters are sibling scope. Native Windows refuses every\n44|// request. No test in this package starts a tmux process: every\n45|// broker, server, and spawner interaction runs through injected\n46|// dependencies, and the suite passes with no tmux installed.\n47|package tmuxserver","final_result":true}}}
