{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c69f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c40c-7a6a-7610-adaa-109852fda585"},"sequence":426,"recorded_at":1780531400000847,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2"},"call_id":"call_01a0c40d7df371d0a93264188bb3759f","text":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/acquire.go`.\n1|package tmuxserver\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axerror\"\n5|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axpane\"\n6|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n7|)\n8|\n9|// Caller names the acquisition caller. The vocabulary is owned by\n10|// internal/axpane, which already gates the wrapper decision over it;\n11|// this package reuses its constants rather than retyping them.\n12|type Caller = string\n13|\n14|const (\n15|\t// CallerForeground is an interactive operator-side caller that\n16|\t// may create the dedicated server.\n17|\tCallerForeground = axpane.CallerForeground\n18|\t// CallerBackground is a background CLI, SSH RPC process,\n19|\t// daemon, or restore worker: it must never create a\n20|\t// credential-dependent tmux server, may contact an\n21|\t// already-running authenticated broker, and otherwise receives\n22|\t// capability_unavailable with no fallback to direct creation.\n23|\tCallerBackground = axpane.CallerBackground\n24|)\n25|\n26|// Acquisition outcomes name how the caller reached the dedicated\n27|// server. Exactly one applies; there is no combined or fallback\n28|// outcome.\n29|const (\n30|\t// ViaSpawned created the dedicated -S server on the foreground\n31|\t// path and returns its spawn argv.\n32|\tViaSpawned = \"spawned\"\n33|\t// ViaAttachedFound the dedicated server already running and\n34|\t// attested on the foreground path.\n35|\tViaAttached = \"attached-running\"\n36|\t// ViaBroker contacted the already-running authenticated Aqua\n37|\t// broker and its attested AX tmux server on the background\n38|\t// path. No local spawn argv exists on this path.\n39|\tViaBroker = \"broker\"\n40|)\n41|\n42|// realmCapability is the Section 4.D capability the background\n43|// typed refusal names: the exact instance passes the AX sentinel\n44|// and the provider-auth smoke without UI. The admission verdict is\n45|// the landed terminalbackend owner's; this package consumes it\n46|// through RealmAdmission and never re-decides it.\n47|const realmCapability = \"credential_capable_execution_realm\"\n48|\n49|// ServerReport is the live dedicated-server probe result: whether\n50|// the private socket answers, with the landed admission verdict over\n51|// the exact server when it does.\n52|type ServerReport struct {\n53|\tRunning   bool\n54|\tAdmission RealmAdmission\n55|}\n56|\n57|// Dependencies carries every external interaction acquisition\n58|// performs. This leaf ships the decision core and argv only: no\n59|// production probe or spawner implementation exists in the tree. The\n60|// exec/probe adapters — which report Reconcile/ResolveEvidence\n61|// verdicts and spawn through the built argv — and the server socket's\n62|// crash evidence are owned by the lifecycle leaf TASK-260830-1c28dz;\n63|// tests wire fakes. No probe runs without its dependency: a nil entry\n64|// refuses instead of reaching for a default.\n65|type Dependencies struct {\n66|\t// ProbeServer reports the dedicated socket's live state.\n67|\tProbeServer func(socket string) (ServerReport, error)\n68|\t// ProbeBroker reports the live Aqua broker state.\n69|\tProbeBroker func() (BrokerReport, error)\n70|\t// Spawn creates the dedicated server with the given -S argv.\n71|\tSpawn func(socket string, argv []string) error\n72|}\n73|\n74|// Request is the complete acquisition surface. There is deliberately\n75|// no member for a credential flag, a managername hint, or a cached\n76|// observation: the background creation rule needs no credential flag\n77|// because the background path never creates on any platform, and a\n78|// hint or cached observation never authorizes, so none is an input.\n79|type Request struct {\n80|\tCaller   Caller\n81|\tPlatform scalar.Platform\n82|\t// Root and Name select the runtime directory: Root is the AX\n83|\t// state root, Name is the runtime leaf (usually\n84|\t// RuntimeDirName). Foreground acquisition ensures the directory\n85|\t// idempotently; background acquisition verifies the existing\n86|\t// directory and never creates it.\n87|\tRoot string\n88|\tName string\n89|\t// Ambient carries the observed ambient socket facts for\n90|\t// evidence. Resolution never reads them; tests assert the\n91|\t// acquired socket equals none of them.\n92|\tAmbient Ambient\n93|\t// SocketOverride must be empty. Any caller-supplied socket —\n94|\t// whichever ambient vector supplied it — refuses.\n95|\tSocketOverride string\n96|\t// SessionID is the logical session the spawned server will\n97|\t// host, as canonical UUIDv7. It shapes spawn argv only.\n98|\tSessionID string\n99|\t// Generation, BrokerState, and Remediation are the typed\n100|\t// realm/readiness details the capability_unavailable refusal\n101|\t// carries. All three are required: an input that omits one\n102|\t// is malformed and refuses invalid_arguments instead of\n103|\t// emitting an untyped refusal. Generation is also the typed\n104|\t// generation every admission must bind to.\n105|\tGeneration  string\n106|\tBrokerState string\n107|\tRemediation string\n108|\tDeps        Dependencies\n109|}\n110|\n111|// Outcome is the one acquisition result.\n112|type Outcome struct {\n113|\tVia    string\n114|\tSocket string\n115|\t// Argv is the dedicated -S spawn argv. It is set only for\n116|\t// ViaSpawned: the broker path spawns nothing and the\n117|\t// attached path presents through sibling-owned attach\n118|\t// semantics, not through a second spawn vector.\n119|\tArgv []string\n120|}\n121|\n122|// Acquire resolves the dedicated server socket from the runtime\n123|// directory and reaches the server through the caller-appropriate\n124|// path. Foreground attaches to the running attested server or\n125|// spawns the dedicated -S server; background contacts the\n126|// already-running authenticated broker or receives the typed\n127|// capability_unavailable refusal, and never falls back to direct\n128|// server creation — there is no spawn call on the background path,\n129|// and every background test arms a spy spawner that fails the run\n130|// if it is ever invoked.\n131|//\n132|// Refusals precede side effects: malformed input, ambient reuse, and\n133|// missing dependencies all refuse before any directory is created,\n134|// and background acquisition verifies the runtime directory without\n135|// creating it, so a background caller performs no durable write.\n136|func Acquire(req Request) (Outcome, error) {\n137|\tif req.Caller != CallerForeground && req.Caller != CallerBackground {\n138|\t\treturn Outcome{}, &Error{Code: CodeInvalidArguments, Detail: \"caller\"}\n139|\t}\n140|\tif req.Generation == \"\" || req.BrokerState == \"\" || req.Remediation == \"\" {\n141|\t\treturn Outcome{}, &Error{Code: CodeInvalidArguments, Detail: \"realm details\"}\n142|\t}\n143|\tdir, err := lexicalRuntimePath(req.Root, req.Name, req.Platform)\n144|\tif err != nil {\n145|\t\treturn Outcome{}, err\n146|\t}\n147|\tsocket, err := ResolveSocket(dir, req.SocketOverride, req.Ambient)\n148|\tif err != nil {\n149|\t\treturn Outcome{}, err\n150|\t}\n151|\tif req.Caller == CallerBackground {\n152|\t\treturn acquireBackground(req, socket)\n153|\t}\n154|\treturn acquireForeground(req, socket)\n155|}\n156|\n157|// acquireBackground implements the broker-or-refuse rule: it may\n158|// contact the already-running authenticated broker and its attested\n159|// server, and when neither exists it returns capability_unavailable\n160|// with typed realm/readiness details. Direct server creation is not\n161|// the else branch — this function has no path to the spawner, on\n162|// any platform — and the runtime directory is verified, never\n163|// created here.\n164|func acquireBackground(req Request, socket string) (Outcome, error) {\n165|\tif req.Deps.ProbeBroker == nil {\n166|\t\treturn Outcome{}, &Error{Code: CodeInvalidArguments, Detail: \"dependencies\"}\n167|\t}\n168|\tif verr := VerifyRuntimeDir(req.Root, req.Name, req.Platform); verr != nil {\n169|\t\treturn Outcome{}, verr\n170|\t}\n171|\tstatus, err := req.Deps.ProbeBroker()\n172|\tif err != nil {\n173|\t\treturn Outcome{}, err\n174|\t}\n175|\tif err := CheckBrokerContact(status, req.Generation, currentUID()); err != nil {\n176|\t\t// The miss path creates nothing: it consults the creation\n177|\t\t// gate so the no-fallback rule is enforced by a call, not\n178|\t\t// by the absence of one. The gate refuses every background\n179|\t\t// caller; its refusal is expected here and the path reports\n180|\t\t// the typed unavailable the spec names. The else branch is\n181|\t\t// reachable only when the gate is weakened to admit a\n182|\t\t// background caller, and then it refuses with the creation\n183|\t\t// code instead of the typed unavailable, so the committed\n184|\t\t// background-miss tests redden.\n185|\t\tif cerr := checkCreationAllowed(req.Caller); cerr != nil {\n186|\t\t\treturn Outcome{}, backgroundUnavailable(req, err)\n187|\t\t}\n188|\t\treturn Outcome{}, &Error{Code: CodeBackgroundCreationRefused, Detail: \"background fallback\"}\n189|\t}\n190|\treturn Outcome{Via: ViaBroker, Socket: socket}, nil\n191|}\n192|\n193|// acquireForeground attaches to the running attested dedicated\n194|// server or spawns it. A running but unattested server refuses:\n195|// acquisition never attaches to a server whose landed admission is\n196|// missing or bound to another generation, and never repairs it here\n197|// — lifecycle owns that decision.\n198|func acquireForeground(req Request, socket string) (Outcome, error) {\n199|\tif req.Deps.ProbeServer == nil || req.Deps.Spawn == nil {\n200|\t\treturn Outcome{}, &Error{Code: CodeInvalidArguments, Detail: \"dependencies\"}\n201|\t}\n202|\tensured, err := EnsureRuntimeDir(req.Root, req.Name, req.Platform, nil)\n203|\tif err != nil {\n204|\t\treturn Outcome{}, err\n205|\t}\n206|\treport, err := req.Deps.ProbeServer(socket)\n207|\tif err != nil {\n208|\t\treturn Outcome{}, err\n209|\t}\n210|\tif report.Running {\n211|\t\tif err := CheckServerAttested(report.Admission, req.Generation); err != nil {\n212|\t\t\treturn Outcome{}, err\n213|\t\t}\n214|\t\treturn Outcome{Via: ViaAttached, Socket: socket}, nil\n215|\t}\n216|\targv, err := BuildArgv(ensured, socket, req.SessionID)\n217|\tif err != nil {\n218|\t\treturn Outcome{}, err\n219|\t}\n220|\tif err := req.Deps.Spawn(socket, argv); err != nil {\n221|\t\treturn Outcome{}, &Error{Code: CodeSpawnFailed, Detail: \"server spawn\"}\n222|\t}\n223|\treturn Outcome{Via: ViaSpawned, Socket: socket, Argv: argv}, nil\n224|}\n225|\n226|// checkCreationAllowed is the single choke point before every\n227|// direct server creation. A background caller never creates: on\n228|// macOS because server creation is credential-sensitive, and on\n229|// every platform because the background path must not fall back to\n230|// direct creation. The macOS credential-dependent case is one\n231|// fixture of this gate, not a narrower arm: narrowing the gate to\n232|// macOS or to credential-dependent servers would admit background\n233|// creation the no-fallback rule forbids. Foreground creation is\n234|// allowed on every platform; the credential binding it needs is\n235|// proven by the landed admission the server must present before\n236|// any attach.\n237|func checkCreationAllowed(caller Caller) error {\n238|\tif caller == CallerBackground {\n239|\t\treturn &Error{Code: CodeBackgroundCreationRefused, Detail: \"background creation\"}\n240|\t}\n241|\treturn nil\n242|}\n243|\n244|// backgroundUnavailable composes the typed capability_unavailable\n245|// refusal the spec names for the background miss, with the exact\n246|// Section 15.3 detail set. The constructor enforces the typed\n247|// details; a failure to render them is itself malformed input, not\n248|// an untyped refusal.\n249|func backgroundUnavailable(req Request, cause error) error {\n250|\tdetails := axerror.RealmEvidence{\n251|\t\tCapability:           realmCapability,\n252|\t\tCallerRealm:          req.Caller,\n253|\t\tBrokerState:          req.BrokerState,\n254|\t\tTmuxServerGeneration: req.Generation,\n255|\t\tRemediation:          req.Remediation,\n256|\t}\n257|\tfailure, err := axerror.NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable(axerror.Version130,\n258|\t\t\"no authenticated broker or attested tmux server\",\n259|\t\taxerror.NoIDs(), details, cause)\n260|\tif err != nil {\n261|\t\treturn &Error{Code: CodeInvalidArguments, Detail: \"realm details\"}\n262|\t}\n263|\treturn failure\n264|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6a1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c40c-7a6a-7610-adaa-109852fda585"},"sequence":427,"recorded_at":1780531400000849,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2"},"call_id":"call_01a0c40d7f65723d8798501971d1ed64","text":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# TRACEABILITY — internal/tmuxserver (AX v0.7.0)\n2|\n3|Normative scope: AX v0.7.0 Section 4.2 (tmux backend: dedicated -S\n4|server, no ambient/default discovery or reuse, credential-sensitive\n5|creation, background broker-or-refuse with typed capability_unavailable\n6|and no fallback to direct creation, launchctl managername as diagnostic\n7|hint only, cached observations never authorize resume), Section 4.C\n8|(operation vocabulary cited for the wrapper entrypoint shape only),\n9|Section 4.D (capability evidence cited landed), and Section 4.E\n10|(sensitive runtime state is owner-only and non-replicable). Story:\n11|production-tmux-backend (first leaf).\n12|\n13|Rule: every row names its production entry point. A row is driven only\n14|when the named committed test executes that entry. Prose in place of\n15|the ratio is not evidence. 55 of 55 AC rows driven (row 55 extends\n16|the rows 19-22 override class with the fifth ambient member,\n17|TMUX_TMPDIR); no row is a bound — the stated bounds below cover\n18|deliberately unclaimed surfaces, not undriven rows.\n19|\n20|No test in this package starts a tmux process: every broker, server,\n21|and spawner interaction runs through injected dependencies, and the\n22|suite passes with no tmux installed. No row has a real-tmux witness;\n23|that is the determinism design, not a gap (bound B1).\n24|\n25|Attestation authority: the sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature\n26|verification, liveness, and expiry verdict is the landed\n27|internal/terminalbackend Reconcile/ResolveEvidence admission,\n28|consumed here as an Admitted set composed only with the generation\n29|equality the wrapper owner (internal/axpane checkRealm) already\n30|enforces. This leaf decides membership plus generation binding and\n31|re-decides nothing the admission proves.\n32|\n33|## Runtime custody (Sections 4.2, 4.E)\n34|\n35|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n36||---|--------|-----------|------|\n37|| 1 | Ensure creates the owner-only 0700 directory, explicitly under a restrictive umask | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go, runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirCreatesOwnerOnly, TestEnsureRuntimeDirEnforcesModeUnderRestrictiveUmask |\n38|| 2 | Re-ensure is idempotent and verifies mode | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go, runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirIsIdempotent |\n39|| 3 | Compliant directory verifies | VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime.go, runtime_unix.go) | TestVerifyRuntimeDirAdmitsCompliant |\n40|| 4 | Widened mode refuses on ensure and verify, never silently repaired | EnsureRuntimeDir, VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesWidenedMode |\n41|| 5 | Non-directory leaf refuses | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf |\n42|| 6 | Symlink leaf refuses on commit and verify | EnsureRuntimeDir, VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkLeaf, TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkLeaf |\n43|| 7 | Foreign ownership refuses on ensure and verify | EnsureRuntimeDir, VerifyRuntimeDir (ownership_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesForeignOwnership |\n44|| 8 | Handle/path mismatch refuses | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesHandleMismatch |\n45|| 9 | Symlinked root refuses | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkRoot |\n46|| 10 | Relative, empty, parent, and missing roots refuse | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesBadRoots (4 subtests) |\n47|| 11 | Empty, dot, parent, nested, absolute, and NUL names refuse | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesBadNames (6 subtests) |\n48|| 12 | Unknown platform refuses | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesBadPlatform |\n49|| 13 | Verify refuses absence without creating | VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesAbsence |\n50|| 14 | Linux and WSL2 share the unix custody discipline | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestLinuxAndWSL2ShareUnixCustody |\n51|| 15 | Windows platform refuses on every host; no tmux directory exists on Windows | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesWindowsOnUnixHost, TestAcquireRefusesWindowsPlatform |\n52|\n53|## Dedicated socket and ambient non-use (Section 4.2)\n54|\n55|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n56||---|--------|-----------|------|\n57|| 16 | Socket derives only from the runtime directory | SocketPath (socket.go) | TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir |\n58|| 17 | Resolution returns the derived socket under hostile ambient on all five members | ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestResolveSocketDerivesIgnoringAmbient |\n59|| 18 | Ambient observation records without using, including nil lookup | ObserveAmbient (socket.go) | TestObserveAmbientRecordsWithoutUsing, TestObserveAmbientNilLookupKeepsOutOfBand |\n60|| 19 | TMUX environment value as override refuses through Acquire with no spawn and no directory | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/environment_variable |\n61|| 20 | Inherited socket as override refuses through Acquire with no spawn and no directory | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/inherited_socket |\n62|| 21 | Default path as override refuses through Acquire with no spawn and no directory | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/default_path |\n63|| 22 | Conventional name as override refuses through Acquire with no spawn and no directory | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/conventional_name |\n64|| 23 | Ambient value colliding with the derived socket refuses on every member | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollision (5 subtests), TestResolveSocketRefusesAmbientCollision (5 subtests) |\n65|| 55 | TMUX_TMPDIR value as override refuses through Acquire with no spawn and no directory | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/tmux_tmpdir |\n66|\n67|## Background broker-or-refuse (Section 4.2)\n68|\n69|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n70||---|--------|-----------|------|\n71|| 24 | Authenticated same-user broker plus generation-bound attested server contacts on macOS, with no spawn and no argv | Acquire (acquire.go) via CheckBrokerContact (readiness.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundContactsBroker |\n72|| 25 | No broker returns the typed capability_unavailable with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/no_broker |\n73|| 26 | Foreign-user broker returns the typed capability_unavailable with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/foreign-user_broker |\n74|| 27 | Unattested server returns the typed capability_unavailable with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/unattested_server |\n75|| 28 | Stale-generation admission returns the typed capability_unavailable with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/stale_server_admission, TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/generation-unbound_principal |\n76|| 29 | Linux miss also returns the typed capability_unavailable with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundMissOnLinuxAlsoRefusesWithoutFallback |\n77|| 30 | Broker probe failure passes through as unknown, never unavailable, with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundProbeFailurePassesThrough |\n78|| 31 | Creation gate refuses the background caller; the miss path enforces it by call | checkCreationAllowed via Acquire (acquire.go) | TestCheckCreationAllowedRefusesBackground, TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable (kill path of N-creation-literal) |\n79|\n80|## Readiness non-authorization (Sections 4.2, 4.D)\n81|\n82|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n83||---|--------|-----------|------|\n84|| 32 | A stale admission replayed on a broker miss still returns the typed capability_unavailable: cached proof authorizes nothing | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/stale_server_admission |\n85|| 33 | A stale admission fakes no running attested server on the foreground path | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireForegroundRefusesWrongGenerationAdmission |\n86|| 34 | Bound admitted row admits | CheckServerAttested (readiness.go) | TestCheckServerAttestedAdmitsBound |\n87|| 35 | Missing realm row refuses, including a decoy capability | CheckServerAttested (readiness.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestCheckServerAttestedRefusesEachMissingConjunct (no admission rows, decoy capability only), TestAcquireForegroundRefusesRunningUnattested |\n88|| 36 | Wrong-generation admission refuses | CheckServerAttested (readiness.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestCheckServerAttestedRefusesEachMissingConjunct (stale generation admission), TestAcquireForegroundRefusesWrongGenerationAdmission, TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/stale_server_admission |\n89|| 37 | Foreign-user broker principal refuses | CheckBrokerContact (readiness.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact (no broker, foreign-user broker), TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/foreign-user_broker |\n90|| 38 | Generation-unbound broker principal refuses | CheckBrokerContact (readiness.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact (generation-unbound and empty principal), TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/generation-unbound_principal |\n91|| 39 | Complete broker report admits | CheckBrokerContact (readiness.go) | TestCheckBrokerContactAdmitsLiveReport |\n92|\n93|## Foreground acquisition (Section 4.2)\n94|\n95|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n96||---|--------|-----------|------|\n97|| 40 | Absent server spawns dedicated with exact -S argv disjoint from every ambient vector and the ax pane tail | Acquire (acquire.go) via BuildArgv (argv.go) | TestAcquireForegroundSpawnsDedicatedServer |\n98|| 41 | Running attested server attaches with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireForegroundAttachesToRunningAttested |\n99|| 42 | Running unattested server refuses with no spawn and no repair | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireForegroundRefusesRunningUnattested |\n100|| 43 | Server probe failure passes through as unknown with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireForegroundProbeFailurePassesThrough |\n101|| 44 | Spawn failure reports with exactly one attempt and no fallback | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireForegroundSpawnFailureReportsWithoutFallback |\n102|| 45 | Malformed session refuses before any spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) via BuildArgv (argv.go) | TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession |\n103|\n104|## Spawn argv (Sections 4.2, 4.C)\n105|\n106|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n107||---|--------|-----------|------|\n108|| 46 | Spawn vector is exactly tmux -S socket new-session -d -s session ax pane session | BuildArgv (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvAddressesOnlyTheDerivedSocket |\n109|| 47 | All five ambient sockets refuse | BuildArgv (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvRefusesAmbientSocket (5 subtests) |\n110|| 48 | Malformed sessions refuse the landed UUIDv7 wiring | BuildArgv (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvRefusesMalformedSession |\n111|\n112|## Input validation (Sections 4.2, 15.3)\n113|\n114|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n115||---|--------|-----------|------|\n116|| 49 | Unknown caller refuses | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireRefusesUnknownCaller |\n117|| 50 | Missing generation, broker state, and remediation each refuse | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireRefusesMissingRealmDetails (3 subtests) |\n118|| 51 | Missing dependencies refuse on every nil shape | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireRefusesMissingDependencies, TestAcquireBackgroundNilBrokerWithSpawnRefuses, TestAcquireForegroundNilSpawnWithProbeRefuses |\n119|| 52 | Foreground acquisition ensures the runtime directory idempotently; background verifies without creating | Acquire (acquire.go) via EnsureRuntimeDir/VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime.go) | TestAcquireCreatesRuntimeDirIdempotently, TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating |\n120|\n121|## Crash and idempotency (Sections 4.2, 4.E)\n122|\n123|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n124||---|--------|-----------|------|\n125|| 53 | Real SIGKILL between mkdir and fsync leaves a retry that converges to the one verified directory | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureCrashChildSelfTerminates |\n126|| 54 | Spawn-then-retry attaches to the one server with exactly one spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireForegroundSpawnIsIdempotentAcrossRetry |\n127|\n128|## Mutation battery\n129|\n130|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py`:\n131|40 narrowing rows KILLED, 1 supplementary additive row KILLED\n132|(D-background-fallback, labeled), 1 harmless control SURVIVED, on two\n133|full passes with identical verdicts and one raw log per plant per run.\n134|Row N-deps-foreground kills by panic: the admitted request calls the\n135|nil spawner and the panic fails the test. No token-preserving\n136|source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text, and the\n137|harness executes the behavioral suite (bound B4).\n138|\n139|## Stated bounds\n140|\n141|- B1 Determinism: no row has a real-tmux witness. Every broker, server,\n142|  and spawner interaction runs through injected dependencies; the suite\n143|  passes with no tmux process anywhere. A live-server test would add a\n144|  witness, not a rule, and is sibling scope.\n145|- B2 Windows refusal: native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux (pinned SPEC\n146|  1458). The Windows platform refuses at the lexical gate on every host\n147|  (row 15); the Windows commit/verify arms refuse every platform and\n148|  exist only so the package compiles under GOOS=windows.\n149|- B3 Nil-dependency weakening on the foreground path panics instead of\n150|  misbehaving; the narrowing row pins the refusal and discloses the\n151|  panic kill.\n152|- B4 No gate inspects source text, so no token-preserving mutant\n153|  applies; the harness executes the behavioral suite.\n154|- B5 Attach presentation vectors are sibling scope: attached and broker\n155|  outcomes carry the socket, and only the spawned outcome carries argv.\n156|- B6 Lifecycle operations (create, attach, status, quiesce, stop,\n157|  terminate, restore) belong to the sibling leaves, not to acquisition.\n158|- B7 The handle-mismatch arm stages its race through the sameDirectory\n159|  seam; a true concurrent handle swap is not staged.\n160|- B8 Registry bindings and the digest re-pin belong to the story's\n161|  final leaf; this leaf documents clause coverage here and in the\n162|  conformance matrix only.\n163|- B9 Adapter split: this leaf ships the decision core and argv only. No\n164|  production probe or spawner implementation exists in the tree; the\n165|  exec/probe adapters that report Reconcile/ResolveEvidence verdicts\n166|  and spawn through the built argv, and the server socket's crash\n167|  evidence, are owned by the lifecycle leaf TASK-260830-1c28dz.\n168|- B10 Crash convergence assumes a umask that preserves owner rwx\n169|  (umask & 0700 == 0). Under an owner-bit-stripping umask a leaf\n170|  stranded between mkdirat and the explicit chmod refuses on retry\n171|  instead of converging, because existing leaves verify, never repair.\n172|- B11 A symlinked intermediate component inside the root path is\n173|  followed; only the root's last component refuses (row 9). This\n174|  matches the landed secprim root open and is the same bound.\n175|- B12 The landed argv shape refusal (BuildArgv via secprim.CheckArgv)\n176|  is reachable only by direct call with a non-filesystem runtime dir;\n177|  through Acquire the directory always names a created directory.\n178|- B13 Sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature verification, liveness,\n179|  and expiry are the landed Reconcile admission's verdict, consumed\n180|  here through Has. This leaf decides membership plus generation\n181|  binding only; the host-binding and provider-build cross-bind the\n182|  wrapper evaluates stays with the lifecycle owner.\n183|- B14 The battery assumes a non-root test user for exactly one row:\n184|  N-fchmod-umask admits non-root creates past the explicit chmod, so\n185|  under root it is equivalent to the original and survives. The\n186|  reviewer's same-shaped plant carries the identical assumption.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6a3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c40c-7a6a-7610-adaa-109852fda585"},"sequence":428,"recorded_at":1780531400000851,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2"},"call_id":"call_01a0c40d80d5725eb5865fda5b67221a","text":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/doc.go`.\n1|// Package tmuxserver owns AX private tmux server management: owner-only\n2|// runtime directories and dedicated tmux -S servers with no ambient or\n3|// default-server discovery or reuse. It is the first leaf of the\n4|// production-tmux-backend story.\n5|//\n6|// Normative scope: AX v0.7.0 Section 4.2 (tmux backend, dedicated -S\n7|// server, credential-sensitive creation, background broker-or-refuse,\n8|// launchctl managername as diagnostic hint only, cached observations\n9|// never authorize resume), Section 4.C (operation vocabulary cited for\n10|// the wrapper entrypoint shape only), Section 4.D (capability evidence\n11|// cited landed), and Section 4.E (sensitive runtime state is owner-only\n12|// and non-replicable).\n13|//\n14|// Division of authority (composed, never forked): the caller vocabulary\n15|// (foreground/background) comes from internal/axpane, which already\n16|// gates the wrapper decision over it; the capability_unavailable typed\n17|// refusal comes from internal/axerror.NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable, which\n18|// enforces the exact Section 15.3 detail set; the attestation verdict\n19|// comes from the landed internal/terminalbackend admission\n20|// (Reconcile/ResolveEvidence), consumed here as an Admitted set\n21|// composed only with the generation equality the wrapper owner\n22|// already enforces — sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature\n23|// verification, liveness, and expiry are the admission's verdict, not\n24|// this leaf's; path grammars come from internal/scalar (absolute root,\n25|// relative member, UUIDv7 session); lexical containment comes from\n26|// internal/secprim.Guard; argv shape validation comes from\n27|// internal/secprim.CheckArgv. What this package owns is the composition\n28|// no landed package provides: the descriptor-relative runtime-directory\n29|// commit (mkdirat from a pinned root handle, not a path-string\n30|// MkdirAll), the three independent custody gates (mode, ownership,\n31|// containment), the five-member ambient non-use proof (TMUX and\n32|// TMUX_TMPDIR environment values, inherited socket, default path,\n33|// conventional name), the background broker-or-refuse acquisition path\n34|// with its no-fallback gate over a typed same-user generation-bound\n35|// broker principal, the foreground ensure-then-attach-or-spawn path,\n36|// and the dedicated -S argv builder.\n37|//\n38|// Bounds: no ax CLI surface, no lifecycle operations (create, attach,\n39|// status, quiesce, stop, terminate, restore belong to the sibling\n40|// leaves), no ConPTY process control, no provider process, no mesh\n41|// transport, and no production probe or spawner implementation —\n42|// caller-supplied probes report the landed admission verdicts, and the\n43|// exec/probe adapters are sibling scope. Native Windows refuses every\n44|// request. No test in this package starts a tmux process: every\n45|// broker, server, and spawner interaction runs through injected\n46|// dependencies, and the suite passes with no tmux installed.\n47|package tmuxserver","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
