{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7f9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c40c-7a6a-7610-adaa-109852fda585"},"sequence":599,"recorded_at":1780531400001193,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c40d-c199-77c3-af19-c36d4ab8db1e"},"task_id":"01a0c40d-c199-77c3-af19-c36d4ab8db1e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c40d-c199-77c3-af19-c36d4ab8db1e","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-11-1\",\n  \"command\": \"git diff HEAD -- LOGBOOK.md | head -n 60; echo \\\"===README===\\\"; git diff HEAD -- README.md | head -n 120\",\n  \"description\": \"Show LOGBOOK and README diffs\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"diff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex eed03e1..5768bb7 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -3,6 +3,24 @@\\n > Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n > Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n \\n+## 2026-09-21\\n+\\n+### TASK-260830-35urbp rev2 — Private tmux server management rework (P1 attestation fork + Windows vet, 9 surviving narrowings)\\n+\\n+- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev1 (CHANGES REQUESTED: 2 P1, 4 P2, 4 P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh). P1-A: `runtime_test.go` now carries `//go:build !windows` (it reassigns the unix-only `effectiveUID` seam and uses `syscall.Umask`); `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` is green (exit 0, run firsthand). P1-B: the forked `LiveAttestation`/`CachedObservation`/`ManagerNameHint`/`BrokerStatus` model is DELETED — `RealmAdmission` consumes the landed `terminalbackend.Admitted` verdict composed only with the `RawGeneration == Generation` equality `axpane.checkRealm` enforces, and the broker principal is a typed same-user UID plus generation-bound generation (no bare boolean); `Request.Hint`/`Cached`/`NeedsCredentials` are deleted with no replacement fields. The three reviewer holes now refuse through `Acquire`: wrong-generation foreground attach, wrong-generation broker contact, and a stale admission (the replayed-cached shape) on both paths.\\n+- P2-A: nine surviving narrowings closed with committed killers + shipped rows — `Acquire` commit-phase refusal (`TestAcquireForegroundStagesCommitPhaseCustodyRefusal`, N-acquire-commit-refusal), background verify wiring (`TestAcquireBackgroundStagesVerifyCustodyRefusal`, N-acquire-verify-refusal), verify-side symlink leaf (N-containment-symlink-verify), `TMUX_TMPDIR` override as the fifth vector (row 55, N-override-tmpdir), per-member collisions through `Acquire` (N-collision ×4), TMUX-env argv member (N-argv-tmuxenv), umask-0177 create proving the explicit `Fchmod` (N-fchmod-umask); the unreachable `ObserveAmbient` vocabulary arm is deleted. P2-B: `PlatformWindows` refuses at the lexical gate on every host (`tmux_invalid_arguments`); the Windows commit/verify arms are refusal stubs and the tripwire is deleted. P2-C: the decision-core-only split is a stated bound (B9, exec/probe adapters + socket crash evidence owned by TASK-260830-1c28dz) and the \\\"production wires\\\" sentence is deleted. P2-D: background acquisition verifies instead of ensuring (no durable write on the authorizing path); the dead foreground `checkCreationAllowed` call is deleted.\\n+- P3: results now read the 30 commands from `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` and report firsthand runs; crash convergence states the umask bound (B10); symlinked root intermediates state the secprim-matching bound (B11); the `CheckArgv` arm is covered by direct call with its Acquire-unreachability bound (B12). Battery: 40 narrowing + 1 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED, twice with per-plant raw logs. AC: 55 of 55 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix rev2). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n+\\n+### TASK-260830-35urbp — Private tmux server management (first leaf, STORY-260830-2t4g7i)\\n+\\n+- DELIVERED: `internal/tmuxserver` — the §4.2/§4.C-4.E first leaf over the landed owners: `EnsureRuntimeDir` commits the runtime leaf via `mkdirat` from a pinned root handle with three independent custody gates (containment, exact `0700`, eUID ownership, each refusing alone; existing dirs verified, never repaired); `ResolveSocket` derives the one `-S` socket from the runtime dir and refuses any override on all four ambient vectors (TMUX env, inherited socket, default path, conventional name); `Acquire` attaches/spawns on foreground and brokers-or-refuses on background with the typed `capability_unavailable` (via `axerror.NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable`) and no fallback — the miss path consults the creation gate by call, and every background test arms a zero-call spy spawner; `CheckLiveAttestation` admits only complete live sentinel+smoke bound to generation/build/macOS, while the managername hint and cached observations travel diagnostics-only and authorize nothing; `BuildArgv` emits the exact `tmux -S socket new-session -d -s session ax pane session` vector through the landed argv gate. No test starts tmux: all probes/spawns are injected fakes.\\n+- F1: a structural absence (\\\"this path has no spawn call\\\") is not an enforceable gate until a call exists to weaken — the background miss path now consults `checkCreationAllowed` by call so the N-creation-literal narrowing (background admitted) reddens through the entry with the creation code instead of the typed unavailable, and the D-background-fallback additive plant (reviewer-shaped direct-creation call) reddens on the spy assertions.\\n+- F2: `Fchmod` before verification silently repairs — the create path now chmods only leaves it created (`Mkdirat` success, for umask) while pre-existing leaves verify as-is, so a widened `0755` refuses on both ensure and verify instead of being narrowed back.\\n+- F3: single-member refusal classes still narrow honestly — `caller == \\\"background\\\"` weakens to the capitalized twin (gate present, one member admitted), and delegated wirings (scalar UUIDv7/platform/path grammars) narrow at our call site with reroute kills, never by re-testing the owner.\\n+- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 29 narrowing mutants plus one supplementary additive row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 31/31 with the harmless SURVIVED control on two full passes, verdict lists identical), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical. No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text. Suite: 89 subtests green, 87.5% statement coverage; `GOOS=windows` builds.\\n+- AC: 54 of 54 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`); crash/idempotency evidence via real SIGKILL between mkdir and fsync plus spawn-then-retry convergence. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n+- BOUNDS: no real-tmux witness for any row (determinism design); Windows ownership is the creating-user ACL (tripwire-pinned); attach presentation vectors and lifecycle operations are sibling-leaf scope; registry bindings and the digest re-pin belong to the final leaf.\\n+\\n ## 2026-09-18\\n \\n ### TASK-260830-32ypr2 — projection fidelity over captured bytes (FINAL leaf, STORY-260830-1cyj0q)\\n===README===\\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex c44349b..2396666 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -2326,6 +2326,60 @@ adds no `ax` command, no `doctor` result, and no runtime capability\\n claim; the clause-to-test matrix with its stated bounds lives in\\n [the task evidence map](internal/termbind/TRACEABILITY.md).\\n \\n+## Private tmux server management (`tmuxserver` leaf)\\n+\\n+[`internal/tmuxserver`](internal/tmuxserver) creates owner-only runtime\\n+directories and manages dedicated `tmux -S` servers with no ambient or\\n+default-server discovery or reuse (pinned Sections 4.2, 4.C-4.E).\\n+`EnsureRuntimeDir` commits the runtime leaf relative to a pinned root\\n+handle (`mkdirat`, never a path-string `MkdirAll`) and enforces three\\n+independent custody gates — containment, exact `0700` mode, effective-UID\\n+ownership — each of which refuses alone; an existing directory is\\n+verified, never silently repaired. `ResolveSocket` derives the one\\n+server socket from the runtime directory and refuses any explicit\\n+override on all five ambient members (`TMUX` and `TMUX_TMPDIR`\\n+environment values, inherited socket, default path, conventional\\n+`default` name). `Acquire` reaches the server through the\\n+caller-appropriate path: foreground ensures the directory, then attaches\\n+to the running attested server or spawns the dedicated `-S` server whose\\n+stable pane entrypoint is `ax pane SESSION_ID`, while background\\n+verifies the existing directory without creating it, contacts only the\\n+already-running authenticated same-user broker and its attested server,\\n+and otherwise returns the typed `capability_unavailable` refusal with\\n+realm/readiness details — there is no fallback to direct creation, and\\n+every background test arms a spy spawner that fails the run if it is\\n+ever invoked. Attestation is the landed `terminalbackend`\\n+Reconcile/ResolveEvidence admission consumed as an `Admitted` set\\n+composed only with generation equality: a missing realm row or a\\n+stale-generation admission refuses, so a cached observation replayed as\\n+live authorizes nothing. Every broker, server, and spawner interaction\\n+runs through injected dependencies, so the suite passes with no tmux\\n+process anywhere; native Windows refuses every request.\\n+\\n+Run the focused tests and coverage with:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1\\n+go test ./internal/tmuxserver -cover -count=1\\n+```\\n+\\n+Run the narrowing battery (40 narrowing mutants, one supplementary\\n+additive row, plus one harmless control) with:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py\\n+```\\n+\\n+The harness mutates one production file in place, runs the named killer\\n+through the production entry point, restores the file from backup, and\\n+reports per-row verdicts with subprocess exits; `AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1`\\n+additionally prints the raw per-plant logs, and `--log-dir` captures one\\n+raw log per plant. Task validation logs and mutation artifacts are\\n+attached to `TASK-260830-35urbp`. The package adds no `ax` command, no\\n+`doctor` result, and no runtime capability claim; the clause-to-test\\n+matrix with its stated bounds lives in\\n+[the task evidence map](internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md).\\n+\\n ## Ownership reducer properties\\n \\n The four story-pinned ownership invariants (pinned v0.6.0 Sections 2.2, 5.3,\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 9794,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2449,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
