{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c951","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c40c-7a6a-7610-adaa-109852fda585"},"sequence":771,"recorded_at":1780531400001537,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"be2f90a4-329e-4dfe-906d-93614b40b7f2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c40e-fab6-7752-85e5-a9ca93c2792c"},"task_id":"01a0c40e-fab6-7752-85e5-a9ca93c2792c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c40e-fab6-7752-85e5-a9ca93c2792c","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/EPIC-260830-1uwj54_m1-single-host-durability/STORY-260830-2t4g7i_production-tmux-backend/TASK-260830-35urbp_implement-private-tmux-server-management/progress.md`.\n1|## Status\n2|development\n3|\n4|## Review\n5|required\n6|\n7|## Task Class\n8|code\n9|\n10|## Estimate\n11|estimated(fibonacci(8))\n12|\n13|## Blocked By\n14|- TASK-260830-2056mm\n15|- TASK-260830-2uowwk\n16|\n17|## Blocks\n18|- TASK-260830-1c28dz\n19|\n20|## Checklist\n21|- [x] Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Create owner-only runtime directories and dedicated tmux -S servers without ambient/default discovery or reuse\n22|- [x] Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\n23|- [x] README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\n24|- [x] Code written per task description and AC\n25|- [x] Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\n26|- [x] In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n27|- [x] Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\n28|- [ ] Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\n29|- [ ] Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n30|- [x] A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\n31|- [x] Lint clean\n32|- [x] Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\n33|- [x] New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\n34|- [x] Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\n35|- [x] Implementation matches AC\n36|- [x] Solution fits project architecture\n37|- [x] Tests green\n38|- [x] Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read — positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\n39|- [x] If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\n40|\n41|## Notes\n42|spawn workload selection: class=implementation source=explicit policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=muse/muse-spark/max pair_source=explicit match=