 :: Admits exactly unclean spellings of the derived socket past the normalization arm; byte-identical collisions still refuse. Narrowing: the equality gate stays, only Clean is dropped. [exit 1]\\nok: N-realm-empty-want: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the both-empty generation pair past the wanted-empty arm; every pair with a non-empty side still refuses on the inequality (the empty-wanted row keeps a bound Raw, the empty-raw row keeps a bound want). Narrowing, not a delete: the inequality arm stays. [exit 1]\\nok: N-broker-empty-generation: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the both-empty principal pair past the principal-empty arm; every other unbound principal still refuses. Kill reroutes to the server-generation refusal (the empty wanted generation reaches CheckServerAttested), which mismatches the broker-generation detail the row asserts. Through Acquire the pair is unreachable: the typed-details check refuses an empty Generation first. [exit 1]\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 1845,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 462,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
