sal`, N-acquire-commit-refusal), background verify wiring (`TestAcquireBackgroundStagesVerifyCustodyRefusal`, N-acquire-verify-refusal), verify-side symlink leaf (N-containment-symlink-verify), `TMUX_TMPDIR` override as the fifth vector (row 55, N-override-tmpdir), per-member collisions through `Acquire` (N-collision ×4), TMUX-env argv member (N-argv-tmuxenv), umask-0177 create proving the explicit `Fchmod` (N-fchmod-umask); the unreachable `ObserveAmbient` vocabulary arm is deleted. P2-B: `PlatformWindows` refuses at the lexical gate on every host (`tmux_invalid_arguments`); the Windows commit/verify arms are refusal stubs and the tripwire is deleted. P2-C: the decision-core-only split is a stated bound (B9, exec/probe adapters + socket crash evidence owned by TASK-260830-1c28dz) and the \"production wires\" sentence is deleted. P2-D: background acquisition verifies instead of ensuring (no durable write on the authorizing path); the dead foreground `checkCreationAllowed` call is deleted.\n12|- P3: results now read the 30 commands from `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` and report firsthand runs; crash convergence states the umask bound (B10); symlinked root intermediates state the secprim-matching bound (B11); the `CheckArgv` arm is covered by direct call with its Acquire-unreachability bound (B12). Battery: 40 narrowing + 1 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED, twice with per-plant raw logs. AC: 55 of 55 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix rev2). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\n13|\n14|### TASK-260830-35urbp — Private tmux server management (first leaf, STORY-260830-2t4g7i)\n15|\n16|- DELIVERED: `internal/tmuxserver` — the §4.2/§4.C-4.E first leaf over the landed owners: `EnsureRuntimeDir` commits the runtime leaf via `mkdirat` from a pinned root handle with three independent custody gates (containment, exact `0700`, eUID ownership, each refusing alone; existing dirs verified, never repaired); `ResolveSocket` derives the one `-S` socket from the runtime dir and refuses any override on all four ambient vectors (TMUX env, inherited socket, default path, conventional name); `Acquire` attaches/spawns on foreground and brokers-or-refuses on background with the typed `capability_unavailable` (via `axerror.NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable`) and no fallback — the miss path consults the creation gate by call, and every background test arms a zero-call spy spawner; `CheckLiveAttestation` admits only complete live sentinel+smoke bound to generation/build/macOS, while the managername hint and cached observations travel diagnostics-only and authorize nothing; `BuildArgv` emits the exact `tmux -S socket new-session -d -s session ax pane session` vector through the landed argv gate. No test starts tmux: all probes/spawns are injected fakes.\n17|- F1: a structural absence (\"this path has no spawn call\") is not an enforceable gate until a call exists to weaken — the background miss path now consults `checkCreationAllowed` by call so the N-creation-literal narrowing (background admitted) reddens through the entry with the creation code instead of the typed unavailable, and the D-background-fallback additive plant (reviewer-shaped direct-creation call) reddens on the spy assertions.\n18|- F2: `Fchmod` before verification silently repairs — the create path now chmods only leaves it created (`Mkdirat` success, for umask) while pre-existing leaves verify as-is, so a widened `0755` refuses on both ensure and verify instead of being narrowed back.\n19|- F3: single-member refusal classes still narrow honestly — `caller == \"background\"` weakens to the capitalized twin (gate present, one member admitted), and delegated wirings (scalar UUIDv7/platform/path grammars) narrow at our call site with reroute kills, never by re-testing the owner.\n20|- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 29 narrowing mutants plus one supplementary additive row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 31/31 with the harmless SURVIVED control on two full passes, verdict lists identical), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical. No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text. Suite: 89 subtests green, 87.5% statement coverage; `GOOS=windows` builds.\n21|- AC: 54 of 54 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`); crash/idempotency evidence via real SIGKILL between mkdir and fsync plus spawn-then-retry convergence. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n22|- BOUNDS: no real-tmux witness for any row (determinism design); Windows ownership is the creating-user ACL (tripwire-pinned); attach presentation vectors and lifecycle operations are sibling-leaf scope; registry bindings and the digest re-pin belong to the final leaf.\n23|\n24|## 2026-09-18\n25|\n26|### TASK-260830-32ypr2 — projection fidelity over captured bytes (FINAL leaf, STORY-260830-1cyj0q)\n27|\n28|- DELIVERED: `internal/cloneproject` implements the Section 13.14.1 projection-fidelity closure — `Normalize` derives a Canonical Session + Canonical Events from a sealed Clone Capture Manifest, its sealed Clone Raw Object Manifest, and blob bytes fetched through the real store layout. Unknown native types and unknown-class members become raw-addressable `opaque_event` records (`unknown_native_event`, ranges resolve to exact bytes); foreign encrypted/signed reasoning becomes byte-exact `opaque_reasoning` (`foreign_encrypted_payload`/`foreign_signature_unverifiable`, no content members); foreign instructions pin `low` authority and never reach the effective snapshot; tool calls resolve `completed` only with their result, else `aborted` history (`unsafe_pending_action`) with an always-empty live surface (pending needs a live work order, which capture never carries); source usage counts source-only; text over 64 KiB becomes an installed overflow blob reference (65536 inline / 65537 referenced, byte-exact). Every proof runs the real `clonesnap.Capture` entry first; every sealed byte re-decodes before return.\n29|- EVIDENCE: package suite green (25 tests incl. the 33-row refusal table plus unstable/drift entries, determinism, idempotent replay, no-partial-bundle failure; 88.9% statement coverage); 49 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED, battery run twice with per-plant raw logs (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`), including two token-preserving rows killed by the behavioral suite and one verified cross-kill (the encrypted-gate plant also reddens the protected-message test). No `ax` command/doctor/capability claim; clause map + per-kind fact registry in `internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n30|- STORY-CLOSE: registry `section:7.8` and `section:10.2` unevidenced→full (2/2 + 5/5, excerpts re-measured, pin re-derived `69d156d9…2235052a` via the gate, shown in results); new acceptance cases `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`, `clone-projection-fidelity`, `session-adapter-call-binding`; `tracecheck` green at cases=144, full=4, partial=8, sliver=5, unevidenced=47, clauses 63/569 with `--section 7.8` and `--section 10.2` admitted; `section:13.14.1` deliberately unbound (scanner sees no RFC 2119 line — closed-shape sentences only — so a binding would measure `unmeasured` and fail assigned scope; record lives in the three TRACEABILITY files + matrices). Pin tests updated (report wants, sliver tables, 10.2 rename row now attacks `Capture`, admits lists extended to 7.8/10.2, README figure pins with `twelve`/`forty-seven`); README package section + measured-coverage rewrite (fenced line byte-equal).\n31|- REFRESH: this run opened on stale base `a12d1bd` (branch tip `47294bb`) while trunk was `c3aae73`, so `refresh-candidate` ran FIRST (`refresh_advanced` onto `c3aae73`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay keeping trunk's 4qojoz entry newest-first). The audit restored trunk bytes for every carried stale revert (`.task-board`, `internal/meshneg`, `internal/rpcwire` tests/harness, `internal/matjournal` test, `task-board.config.json` back to the 30-command form); README/LOGBOOK/traceability edits were re-applied purely additively on the new bytes and the ownership registry MERGED (trunk's 5 cases + 3 upgraded bindings kept, this story's 4 cases + 2 bindings appended/transplanted — never replaced). Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 7 bounded groups incl. sessquery alone, 41/41 packages, no DATA RACE).\n32|- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): fixture-native record envelope is test-defined framing (body shapes exact, envelope extras unclaimed); fact registries only for emitted kinds; native-protected records carry no reason code; turn IDs/source times null; call arguments not carried; SYNTHESIZED/partial/unavailable statuses and non-text content blocks never emitted (shape rules owned by the accepted clonebundle suite); 13.14.2–13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions, planning, lineage, transaction, tuple admission) sibling-owned; 7.8 operation frames stay `sessadapter`. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\n33|- AC: 24 of 24 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests and measured with narrowings (matrix in `TASK-260830-32ypr2_conformance-matrix.md`).\n34|- REV2 (rework of review RUN-260918-320878, CHANGES REQUESTED; no base move, still `3005d78` over trunk `c3aae73`): P1-a CLOSED — envelope+body frame decodes delegate to `environ.DecodeStrictObject` at `strictMembers` (lone-surrogate/duplicate/trailing faults refuse with the fault named; the later struct read is exact because the rewriting/guessing shapes never pass the gate); 4 new refusal rows + 4 narrowings. P2-c CLOSED — `bodyUint53` and the envelope version delegate to `environ.CheckUint53Bounds` (string-typed numbers refuse; per-member failures merge into one \"is not a uint53\" refusal while the ledger sum keeps \"exceeds uint53\"); string rows + 5 narrowings. New P3 rows: actor-order determinism (3 actors x12, `N-actors-sort`), both type/protection agreement arms, trailing bytes, protected-tool fold-skip, result-status vocabulary, size arm with its own message + drift row, unknown+protected body refusal; P3-i non-JSONL bound stated + pinned, P3-l null-directives pinned, P3-c per-edge rows stated as bounds (the \"representative\" claim removed); P3-j unions the 10.2 binding to 11 cases (10.2#2 gains `localstore-immutable-blob-install`); P3-k relabels (`N-empty-projection` single-member class, `N-overflow-truncate` behaviour swap). P2-a: one decision line per inherited advisory group (1,2,3,5,6,7b deferred with owners; 4/P3-e closed as a stated bound; 7a/P3-ζ closed by P1-a; 7c/P3-ζ′ rewritten as a deferred-unification bound) and the two false-prose sites rewritten. P2-b: 7.8#1 rebound to the new `session-adapter-frame-bound` case (`DecodeRequestFrame` + the oversize/edge tests, sessadapter owner); cases 144→145; digest re-derived `4bd01143…` gate-computed; README prose fixed (7.8 bound to sessadapter, Nine cases, admissions list, 10.2 union note).\n35|- REV2 EVIDENCE: 62 narrowing + 2 labelled rows KILLED + control SURVIVED, battery green twice with per-plant raw logs; the six re-anchorable reviewer plants (R1,R2,R5,R6,R7,R8 shapes) KILLED firsthand by the new tests. AC: 38 of 38 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests (matrix rev2).\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
